  "verdict": "kill",
  "verdict_basis": "Within-band Spearman rho(knn_distance, abs_error) is NEGATIVE in all 5 bands (overall -0.127), with 3 of 5 band CIs excluding zero on the negative side. The decision rule requires POSITIVE within-band rho with CI excluding zero for 'continue', and any positive-CI band for 'train_contrastive'. There are zero positive bands; several are significantly negative. Far-from-fleet windows have slightly LOWER error here \u2014 the reverse of the trust thesis. This is a stronger refutation than flatness: the cheap embedding's geometry carries error information in the WRONG direction, so it does not route to SupCon.",
  "execution_notes_prior_blocked_attempts": {
    "see": "git history commit 6b9b4702 + this file's predecessor",
    "summary": "First design scored ALL test cycles and blocked: C-MAPSS test split has no per-cycle rul_target (13096/13096 NaN). Runs 1-2 were environmental (mlflow missing; sklearn version skew -> pinned 1.4.2). Run 3-4 surfaced the test-truth data fact. Redesigned to Option B (train-split held-out units, real per-cycle truth) and re-ran -> this verdict."
  }
